ploy-integrated/` (the `.rev` file and the `sdk-all*.js` files) inside `external/sdkjs`. The factory then committed those build files as \"uncommitted changes left\", which broke rule R2. I never edited them myself.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- **The bad commit:** I reverted it in `external/sdkjs` with `git revert`. The fork branch now has the same content as `pkt/PKT-0133-base`.\n- **Keeping the build files out:** I added `/deploy-integrated/` to the local `.git/info/exclude` of that checkout. That file isn't tracked, so it doesn't count toward scope. After the profile ran again, `external/sdkjs` was still clean.\n- **The root cause:** fixing it means editing `serve-integrated.sh`, which is outside my target. I recorded a follow-up request under `.theseus/spawn/`: \"Keep serve-integrated build output out of the sdkjs checkout\". Its acceptance check requires the sdkjs checkout to stay clean after the script runs.\n- **Records:** I added an entry to the packet's Executor log, a line to Lessons, and a friction line. My first friction line used the wrong format and `theseus validate` caught it; I rewrote it in the same format as the existing lines, and validate now reports 0 errors.\n\n**Lesson for the Atlas:** any packet that uses the integrated build leaves `deploy-integrated/` behind in `external/sdkjs`. Until the follow-up lands, it has to be excluded there or the factory will commit it.","ttft_ms":2681,"type":"result","duration_ms":689256,"uuid":"585e9e0b-dafe-4d4d-9026-342bfbc292ce","ttft_stream_ms":2036,"time_to_request_ms":340,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":240,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":16,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":6,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":0,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":12,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":6,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":18,"me